.TH ACC-CLI 1 2026-10-22 "ACC" "ACC Manual"
.SH NAME
acc-cli \- operator command line for an ACC collective
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B acc-cli
.RB [ \-v | \-vv ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ACTION ]
.RI [ ARGS ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B acc-cli
is the one-shot operator interface to an ACC (Agentic Cell Corpus)
collective.
It surfaces every internal channel \(em the NATS bus, the LLM backend, the
role loader, the oversight queue, the session tracelog, the knowledge store
\(em through one command, so the same operations a TUI screen offers can be
scripted, run over SSH, or driven from CI.
.PP
Each command lives in its own module and imports its dependencies only when
it runs: a command that never touches the bus (\fBrole list\fR,
\fBconfig show\fR) works on a host where the collective is down.
Without a command,
.B acc-cli
prints its help and exits 0.
.PP
Most read commands accept
.B \-\-json
for machine-readable output.
Commands that change governed state (oversight decisions, role infusion,
configuration, access) act as the principal
.B acc-cli access whoami
reports, and are subject to that principal's ceiling.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase log verbosity: \fB\-v\fR for INFO, \fB\-vv\fR for DEBUG.
Logs go to standard error.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help for
.B acc-cli
or for any command or action and exit.
