.TP
\fB\-\-role\fR \fIROLE\fR
Show the effective view for a role.
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli mcp test\fR \fIserver\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Connect and list tools; report where it fails.
.TP
\fBacc-cli mcp add\fR \fIserver\fR [\fB\-\-url\fR \fIURL\fR] [\fB\-\-transport\fR \fI{http,stdio}\fR] [\fB\-\-api\-key\-env\fR \fIAPI_KEY_ENV\fR] [\fB\-\-purpose\fR \fIPURPOSE\fR]
Register an operator-added server.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-url\fR \fIURL\fR
Base URL (required for http transport).
.TP
\fB\-\-api\-key\-env\fR \fIAPI_KEY_ENV\fR
Env var holding the bearer token.
.TP
\fB\-\-purpose\fR \fIPURPOSE\fR
One-line description.
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli mcp remove\fR \fIserver\fR
Remove an operator-added server.
.TP
\fBacc-cli mcp tools\fR \fIserver\fR [\fB\-\-role\fR \fIROLE\fR] [\fB\-\-enable\fR \fIENABLE\fR] [\fB\-\-disable\fR \fIDISABLE\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Show or gate individual tools.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-role\fR \fIROLE\fR
Show the effective view for a role.
.TP
\fB\-\-enable\fR \fIENABLE\fR
Remove a host-level block.
.TP
\fB\-\-disable\fR \fIDISABLE\fR
Block a tool on this host.
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli mcp enable\fR \fIserver\fR
Re-enable a server on this host.
.TP
\fBacc-cli mcp disable\fR \fIserver\fR
Disable a server on this host.
.TP
\fBacc-cli mcp serve\fR \fB\-\-executor\fR \fIEXECUTOR\fR [\fB\-\-session\fR \fISESSION\fR] [\fB\-\-collective\-id\fR \fICOLLECTIVE_ID\fR] [\fB\-\-nats\-url\fR \fINATS_URL\fR] [\fB\-\-redis\-url\fR \fIREDIS_URL\fR]
Serve ACC to a coding agent over stdio (CS-02): work items, notes, ask.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-executor\fR \fIEXECUTOR\fR
Who is calling: claude-vertex, codex, cursor, ...
.TP
\fB\-\-session\fR \fISESSION\fR
Session id (default: generated).
.TP
\fB\-\-redis\-url\fR \fIREDIS_URL\fR
ACC's Redis (default ACC_REDIS_URL, else redis://localhost:6379).
.RE
.SS "ingest"
Bring a coding agent's session into ACC (CS-05).
.TP
\fBacc-cli ingest session\fR \fB\-\-executor\fR \fIEXECUTOR\fR [\fB\-\-event\fR \fIEVENT\fR] [\fB\-\-transcript\fR \fITRANSCRIPT\fR] [\fB\-\-session\fR \fISESSION\fR] [\fB\-\-cwd\fR \fICWD\fR] [\fB\-\-model\fR \fIMODEL\fR] [\fB\-\-collective\-id\fR \fICOLLECTIVE_ID\fR] [\fB\-\-redis\-url\fR \fIREDIS_URL\fR] [\fB\-\-strict\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Summarise one coding session into ACC's notes.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-executor\fR \fIEXECUTOR\fR
claude-vertex, codex, cursor, ...
.TP
\fB\-\-event\fR \fIEVENT\fR
The hook's JSON event, or '-' to read it from stdin.
.TP
\fB\-\-transcript\fR \fITRANSCRIPT\fR
Transcript file (JSONL or text).
.TP
\fB\-\-session\fR \fISESSION\fR
Session id (else from the event).
.TP
\fB\-\-cwd\fR \fICWD\fR
Working directory (else from the event, else here).
.TP
\fB\-\-model\fR \fIMODEL\fR
models.yaml entry that writes the summary (a local one); default: a digest.
.TP
\fB\-\-redis\-url\fR \fIREDIS_URL\fR
ACC's Redis (default ACC_REDIS_URL, else redis://localhost:6379).
.TP
\fB\-\-strict\fR
Exit non-zero on any error.
.RE
.SS "trace"
Tail NATS for messages mentioning a specific task_id.
.PP
\fBacc-cli trace\fR \fItask_id\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR] [\fB\-n\fR \fILIMIT\fR] [\fB\-\-from\-jetstream\fR]
.RS
.TP
\fItask_id\fR
Task identifier to match in payloads.
.TP
\fB\-\-collective\fR, \fB\-c\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR
Collective to scope the wildcard (default: $ACC_COLLECTIVE_ID).
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR, \fB\-n\fR \fILIMIT\fR
Stop after N matching messages (0 = run until Ctrl-C).
.TP
\fB\-\-from\-jetstream\fR
Replay prior messages from JetStream before tailing live.
.RE
.SS "memory"
Durable memory notes, and erasure.
.TP
\fBacc-cli memory notes\fR [\fB\-\-scope\fR \fISCOPE\fR] [\fB\-\-role\fR \fIROLE\fR] [\fB\-\-hub\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Show the notes a scope would read.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-scope\fR \fISCOPE\fR
Memory scope (default: the operator's own).
.TP
\fB\-\-role\fR \fIROLE\fR
Role whose notes to read.
.TP
\fB\-\-hub\fR
Show the hub's enterprise tier for the role instead (the collective's hub_collective_id).
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli memory propose\fR [\fB\-\-role\fR \fIROLE\fR] [\fB\-\-scope\fR \fISCOPE\fR] [\fB\-\-index\fR \fIINDEX\fR] \fB\-\-to\fR \fITO\fR [\fB\-\-override\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Propose one note for publication into a scope or the hub (hub:<cid>); a person approves.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-role\fR \fIROLE\fR
Role whose note it is.
.TP
\fB\-\-scope\fR \fISCOPE\fR
Scope the note was distilled in.
.TP
\fB\-\-index\fR \fIINDEX\fR
Which note in `memory notes --scope` (0-based).
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR \fITO\fR
Destination: a scope, or hub:<hub collective id>.
.TP
\fB\-\-override\fR
Propose a single-source note anyway (marked; the approver sees it).
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli memory curate\fR [\fB\-\-hub\fR \fIHUB\fR] [\fB\-\-propose\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
The hub curator's job, by hand: which shared notes across the bound instances qualify for the hub.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-hub\fR \fIHUB\fR
Hub collective id (default: this collective's hub_collective_id).
.TP
\fB\-\-propose\fR
Queue a publish proposal for each candidate.
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli memory forget\fR \fB\-\-person\fR \fIPERSON\fR [\fB\-\-apply\fR] [\fB\-\-quorum\fR \fIQUORUM\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-plan\fR] [\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR]
Remove a person's episodes and reconcile the notes drawn from them.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-person\fR \fIPERSON\fR
Requester identity, e.g. slack:U123 (the room is ignored).
.TP
\fB\-\-apply\fR
Actually erase. Without this it is a dry run.
.TP
\fB\-\-quorum\fR \fIQUORUM\fR
People required to keep a note published.
.TP
\fB\-\-plan\fR
Read-only: everything resting on this person across the collectives' refinement ledgers (notes and every copy derived from them). Erases nothing.
.TP
\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR
--plan: a collective whose ledger to read (repeatable; default: this collective and its hub).
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli memory lineage\fR \fI[note_id]\fR [\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR] [\fB\-\-as\fR \fI{turtle,ntriples,jsonld}\fR] [\fB\-\-check\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Where a note came from and everywhere it went, from the refinement ledger (RDF-03).
.RS
.TP
\fI[note_id]\fR
Note id or unique prefix.
.TP
\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR
A collective whose ledger to read (repeatable; default: this collective and its hub).
.TP
\fB\-\-as\fR \fI{turtle,ntriples,jsonld}\fR
Print the lineage as RDF (PROV-O) instead of a tree.
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fR
Report on the projection itself: rows read, notes, copies, and notes something derives from that no ledger row explains.
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli memory export\fR \fB\-\-okf\fR \fIDIR\fR [\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR]
Write the memory you may see as an OKF bundle (open it in Obsidian; RDF-07).
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-okf\fR \fIDIR\fR
Directory to write the bundle into.
.TP
\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR
Collective id (default: this collective).
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Write into a directory that is not empty (files are overwritten).
.RE
.SS "lessons"
Lessons agents shared with each other (KNOWLEDGE_SHARE).
.TP
\fBacc-cli lessons list\fR [\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR \fILIMIT\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Most recent lessons published in the collective.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR
Collective id (default: ACC_COLLECTIVE_ID).
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli lessons show\fR \fIlesson_id\fR [\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-as\fR \fI{turtle,ntriples,jsonld}\fR]
One lesson, in full.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-as\fR \fI{turtle,ntriples,jsonld}\fR
Print the lesson as RDF (persons pseudonymous under ACC_RDF_PERSON_KEY).
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli lessons trace\fR \fIlesson_id\fR [\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
A lesson and every task whose prompt rendered it.
.TP
\fBacc-cli lessons send\fR \fB\-\-to\fR \fITO\fR \fB\-\-text\fR \fITEXT\fR [\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR] [\fB\-\-role\fR \fIROLE\fR] [\fB\-\-scope\fR \fISCOPE\fR] [\fB\-\-ceiling\fR \fICEILING\fR] [\fB\-\-tag\fR \fITAG\fR] [\fB\-\-kind\fR \fI{note,role_patch}\fR] [\fB\-\-patch\-role\fR \fIPATCH_ROLE\fR] [\fB\-\-set\fR \fIFIELD=VALUE\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Publish one lesson addressed to a single agent (relay smoke test).
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR \fITO\fR
Target agent id.
.TP
\fB\-\-text\fR \fITEXT\fR
The lesson, one or two sentences.
.TP
\fB\-\-role\fR \fIROLE\fR
role_label the receiver sees (default: operator).
.TP
\fB\-\-scope\fR \fISCOPE\fR
Memory scope the lesson belongs to (default: local).
.TP
\fB\-\-ceiling\fR \fICEILING\fR
Reader ceiling needed to see it (LOW < MEDIUM < HIGH < CRITICAL; default LOW).
.TP
\fB\-\-tag\fR \fITAG\fR
domain_tag (default: universal).
.TP
\fB\-\-kind\fR \fI{note,role_patch}\fR
note (rendered once) or role_patch (becomes a role_update proposal; Phase 3).
.TP
\fB\-\-patch\-role\fR \fIPATCH_ROLE\fR
role_patch: the role to change (default: the receiver's).
.TP
\fB\-\-set\fR \fIFIELD=VALUE\fR
role_patch: a field to set (repeatable; JSON values accepted).
.RE
.SS "kg"
The collective's knowledge store: named graphs, one ceiling each (RDF-04).
.TP
\fBacc-cli kg sync\fR [\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR]
Rebuild the governed graphs (provenance by ceiling, taxonomy). Operator.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR
Collective (default: ACC_COLLECTIVE_ID / config).
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli kg graphs\fR [\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR] [\fB\-\-ceiling\fR \fICEILING\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
The graphs you may read, with their ceilings.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR
Collective (default: ACC_COLLECTIVE_ID / config).
.TP
\fB\-\-ceiling\fR \fICEILING\fR
Read as if at this ceiling (narrows only).
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli kg query\fR \fIsparql\fR [\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR] [\fB\-\-ceiling\fR \fICEILING\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Run a SPARQL read over the graphs you may read.
.RS
.TP
\fIsparql\fR
SELECT / ASK / CONSTRUCT / DESCRIBE; acc:, prov:, skos: \[u2026] are predeclared.
.TP
\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR
Collective (default: ACC_COLLECTIVE_ID / config).
.TP
\fB\-\-ceiling\fR \fICEILING\fR
Read as if at this ceiling (narrows only).
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli kg infer\fR \fIname\fR \fB\-\-from\fR \fISOURCES\fR [\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR]
RDFS/SKOS closure of some graphs into a new one, at their highest ceiling. Operator.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fISOURCES\fR
A source graph (repeatable).
.TP
\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR
Collective (default: ACC_COLLECTIVE_ID / config).
.RE
.SS "rdf"
Read ACC lessons, tasks, BOMs and OKF concepts as RDF.
.TP
\fBacc-cli rdf vocab\fR [\fB\-\-format\fR \fI{turtle,ntriples,jsonld}\fR]
The ACC vocabulary (every acc: term, described).
.TP
\fBacc-cli rdf context\fR
The JSON-LD @context ACC documents use.
.TP
\fBacc-cli rdf taxonomy\fR [\fB\-\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-pack\fR \fIPACK\fR] [\fB\-\-hub\fR \fIHUB\fR] [\fB\-\-match\fR \fIRECEPTOR TAG\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR \fI{turtle,ntriples,jsonld}\fR]
Check a domain taxonomy (taxonomy/domains.yaml) and print it as SKOS.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR
A domains.yaml file.
.TP
\fB\-\-pack\fR \fIPACK\fR
An installed pack (@scope/name) carrying taxonomy/domains.yaml.
.TP
\fB\-\-hub\fR \fIHUB\fR
The taxonomy a hub collective published (needs Redis).
.TP
\fB\-\-match\fR \fIRECEPTOR TAG\fR
Say whether a receptor hears a lesson tagged TAG, and why.
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli rdf convert\fR \fI{lesson,task,bom,okf}\fR \fIfile\fR [\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR] [\fB\-\-bundle\fR \fIBUNDLE\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR \fI{turtle,ntriples,jsonld}\fR]
Map one file to RDF.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR
task: the collective it ran in.
.TP
\fB\-\-bundle\fR \fIBUNDLE\fR
okf: the bundle name (default: the file's parent dir).
.RE
.SS "refine"
The refinement ledger: every durable change, its evidence, its outcome.
.TP
\fBacc-cli refine list\fR [\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR] [\fB\-\-kind\fR \fIKIND\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR \fILIMIT\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Most recent refinement records.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-kind\fR \fIKIND\fR
One of note, adopt, propose, publish, hub_promote, role_patch, rule, forget, outcome, rollback.
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli refine show\fR \fIrefinement_id\fR [\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
One record in full.
.TP
\fBacc-cli refine trace\fR \fItarget_id\fR [\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Every record about one note / lesson / role id, oldest first.
.TP
\fBacc-cli refine rollback\fR \fIrefinement_id\fR [\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR] [\fB\-\-apply\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Undo one record. Dry run unless --apply.
.SS "msg"
Direct messages to one agent (steer or follow-up).
.TP
\fBacc-cli msg send\fR \fIagent_id\fR \fB\-\-text\fR \fITEXT\fR [\fB\-\-steer\fR] [\fB\-\-follow\-up\fR] [\fB\-\-auto\fR] [\fB\-\-task\fR \fITASK\fR] [\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Send one message to one agent.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-steer\fR
Into the task in flight (a follow-up when nothing is).
.TP
\fB\-\-follow\-up\fR
A new task for the agent, after its current one.
.TP
\fB\-\-auto\fR
Steer if busy, follow-up if idle (default).
.TP
\fB\-\-task\fR \fITASK\fR
The task this is about, if known.
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli msg tail\fR \fIagent_id\fR [\fB\-\-limit\fR \fILIMIT\fR] [\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Receipts for the messages an agent received.
.TP
\fBacc-cli msg show\fR \fImessage_id\fR [\fB\-\-collective\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR]
One message and its receipt.
.SS "sessions"
Read the durable session tracelog (prompts, tool calls, Cat-ABC).
.TP
\fBacc-cli sessions list\fR
List sessions with a tracelog (newest first).
.TP
\fBacc-cli sessions browse\fR \fI[query]\fR [\fB\-\-role\fR \fIROLE\fR] [\fB\-\-since\-days\fR \fISINCE_DAYS\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Search and summarise sessions.
.TP
\fBacc-cli sessions resume\fR \fIsession_id\fR [\fB\-\-context\fR]
Start a new session continuing an old one.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-context\fR
Also print prior context.
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli sessions continue\fR [\fB\-\-context\fR]
Resume the most recent session.
.TP
\fBacc-cli sessions rename\fR \fIsession_id\fR \fItitle\fR
Give a session a title.
.TP
\fBacc-cli sessions export\fR \fIsession_id\fR [\fB\-\-out\fR \fIOUT\fR]
Emit a session as JSONL.
.TP
\fBacc-cli sessions retention\fR [\fB\-\-apply\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Show or apply the retention policy.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-apply\fR
Remove what the policy allows.
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli sessions show\fR \fIsession_id\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Print a session's trace, turn by turn.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit raw JSONL records instead of the summary.
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli sessions verify\fR \fIsession_id\fR
Verify Cat A/B/C were present + evaluated for every turn (exit 1 if incomplete).
.SS "scan"
Scan components for known vulnerabilities.
.PP
\fBacc-cli scan\fR [\fB\-\-package\fR \fIPACKAGE\fR] [\fB\-\-fail\-on\fR \fI{,low,medium,high,critical}\fR] [\fB\-\-propose\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-package\fR \fIPACKAGE\fR
Scan a package manifest's declared dependencies instead of the runtime.
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-on\fR \fI{,low,medium,high,critical}\fR
Exit non-zero when a finding at or above this severity exists.
.TP
\fB\-\-propose\fR
Emit an oversight proposal with the evidence attached.
.RE
.SS "setup"
Guided first-run configuration.
.PP
\fBacc-cli setup\fR \fI[section]\fR [\fB\-\-quick\fR] [\fB\-\-reconfigure\fR] [\fB\-\-answers\fR \fIANSWERS\fR] [\fB\-\-from\-env\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-show\-answers\fR]
.RS
.TP
\fI[section]\fR
Run one section only (posture, model, storage).
.TP
\fB\-\-quick\fR
Only ask for unset values.
.TP
\fB\-\-reconfigure\fR
Ask for everything, including values already set.
.TP
\fB\-\-answers\fR \fIANSWERS\fR
JSON answer set (non-interactive).
.TP
\fB\-\-from\-env\fR
Take answers from ACC_SETUP_* environment variables.
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Validate, write nothing.
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-answers\fR
Print an answer-set template and exit.
.RE
.SS "objective"
Persistent objectives with an operator ceiling.
.TP
\fBacc-cli objective list\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Show objectives.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Include stopped and completed.
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli objective new\fR \fIstatement\fR [\fB\-\-max\-turns\fR \fIMAX_TURNS\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-tokens\fR \fIMAX_TOKENS\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-seconds\fR \fIMAX_SECONDS\fR] [\fB\-\-role\fR \fIROLE\fR] [\fB\-\-owner\fR \fIOWNER\fR]
Create an objective (a ceiling is required).
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-role\fR \fIROLE\fR
Role that pursues it.
.TP
\fB\-\-owner\fR \fIOWNER\fR
Who asked for it.
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli objective show\fR \fIid\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Inspect one objective.
.TP
\fBacc-cli objective pause\fR \fIid\fR
Pause an objective.
.TP
\fBacc-cli objective resume\fR \fIid\fR
Resume a paused objective.
.TP
\fBacc-cli objective cancel\fR \fIid\fR [\fB\-\-reason\fR \fIREASON\fR]
Stop an objective.
.SS "ask"
Give ACC a task and answer its questions inline.
.PP
\fBacc-cli ask\fR \fIprompt [prompt ...]\fR [\fB\-\-role\fR \fIROLE\fR] [\fB\-\-mode\fR \fIMODE\fR] [\fB\-\-session\fR \fISESSION\fR] [\fB\-\-workspace\fR \fIWORKSPACE\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fITIMEOUT\fR] [\fB\-\-collective\-id\fR \fICOLLECTIVE_ID\fR] [\fB\-\-nats\-url\fR \fINATS_URL\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-answer\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
.RS
.TP
\fIprompt [prompt ...]\fR
The task, in your words.
.TP
\fB\-\-role\fR \fIROLE\fR
Target role (default: assistant).
.TP
\fB\-\-mode\fR \fIMODE\fR
Operating mode (default ASK_ONCE, 'Ask once').
.TP
\fB\-\-session\fR \fISESSION\fR
Continue this session (thread).
.TP
\fB\-\-workspace\fR \fIWORKSPACE\fR
Workspace project under /workspace.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fITIMEOUT\fR
Seconds to wait for the answer.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-answer\fR
Print questions but do not answer them (they wait in the queue).
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the final reply as JSON.
.RE
.SS "evals"
promptfoo and Garak attached to a profile.
.TP
\fBacc-cli evals status\fR
Show the evals settings.
.TP
\fBacc-cli evals promptfoo-config\fR \fB\-\-out\fR \fIOUT\fR [\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fIBASE_URL\fR] [\fB\-\-prefix\fR \fIPREFIX\fR] [\fB\-\-root\fR \fIROOT\fR]
Write a promptfoo config from the golden prompts.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR \fIOUT\fR
Where to write promptfooconfig.yaml.
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fIBASE_URL\fR
ACC's OpenAI-compatible endpoint.
.TP
\fB\-\-prefix\fR \fIPREFIX\fR
Only golden prompts whose name starts with this.
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fIROOT\fR
Golden prompt directory.
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli evals garak-gate\fR \fB\-\-report\fR \fIREPORT\fR \fB\-\-baseline\fR \fIBASELINE\fR [\fB\-\-tolerance\fR \fITOLERANCE\fR] [\fB\-\-accept\fR]
Gate a garak report against the baseline.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-report\fR \fIREPORT\fR
garak's report JSONL.
.TP
\fB\-\-baseline\fR \fIBASELINE\fR
Baseline JSON (written by --accept).
.TP
\fB\-\-accept\fR
Make this run the baseline.
.RE
.SS "grants"
Standing grants from repeated approvals (a person gives each).
.TP
\fBacc-cli grants detect\fR [\fB\-\-threshold\fR \fITHRESHOLD\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-window\-days\fR \fIMIN_WINDOW_DAYS\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Repeated approvals worth a standing grant (proposals).
.TP
\fBacc-cli grants accept\fR \fIevidence_hash\fR \fB\-\-by\fR \fIBY\fR [\fB\-\-threshold\fR \fITHRESHOLD\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-window\-days\fR \fIMIN_WINDOW_DAYS\fR]
Give a standing grant for one proposal.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-by\fR \fIBY\fR
Your name: who gives the grant.
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli grants reject\fR \fIevidence_hash\fR [\fB\-\-reason\fR \fIREASON\fR]
Do not propose this evidence again.
.TP
\fBacc-cli grants list\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
List standing grants.
.TP
\fBacc-cli grants revoke\fR \fIgrant_id\fR \fB\-\-by\fR \fIBY\fR
Revoke a standing grant.
.TP
\fBacc-cli grants add\fR \fB\-\-role\fR \fIROLE\fR \fB\-\-target\fR \fITARGET\fR \fB\-\-by\fR \fIBY\fR
Give a grant directly (skill:, mcp: or host: target).
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-role\fR \fIROLE\fR
The role the grant is for (as the dispatcher names it).
.TP
\fB\-\-target\fR \fITARGET\fR
skill:<id> | mcp:<server.tool> | host:<name>[:<port>]
.TP
\fB\-\-by\fR \fIBY\fR
Your name: who gives the grant.
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli grants sync-sandbox\fR
Re-apply active host grants to the OpenShell policy.
.SS "posture"
Agent-configuration posture scan (EC-02).
.TP
\fBacc-cli posture scan\fR [\fB\-\-root\fR \fIROOT\fR] [\fB\-\-sarif\fR \fISARIF\fR] [\fB\-\-fail\-on\fR \fI{LOW,MEDIUM,HIGH,CRITICAL}\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-installed\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Scan roles, agentsets and the environment.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fIROOT\fR
Checkout to scan (default: this one).
.TP
\fB\-\-sarif\fR \fISARIF\fR
Also write a SARIF 2.1.0 log here.
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-on\fR \fI{LOW,MEDIUM,HIGH,CRITICAL}\fR
Exit 1 when a finding is at this severity or worse (default HIGH; the role QA gate uses MEDIUM).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-installed\fR
Scan only this checkout, not the installed packs' roles.
.RE
.SS "mission"
List, close and settle 'ask once' missions.
.TP
\fBacc-cli mission list\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
List missions.
.TP
\fBacc-cli mission patterns\fR [\fB\-\-min\-missions\fR \fIMIN_MISSIONS\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Lesson candidates from closed plans (059): roles planned but not needed, or needed but not planned.
.TP
\fBacc-cli mission show\fR \fImission_id\fR [\fB\-\-by\fR \fIBY\fR] [\fB\-\-host\-dir\fR \fIHOST_DIR\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Show a mission's report.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-by\fR \fIBY\fR
Who closes / revokes it.
.TP
\fB\-\-host\-dir\fR \fIHOST_DIR\fR
Host directory of the agents' /workspace mount (default: $ACC_WORKSPACE_HOST_DIR).
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli mission close\fR \fImission_id\fR [\fB\-\-by\fR \fIBY\fR] [\fB\-\-host\-dir\fR \fIHOST_DIR\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Close a mission and print its report.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-by\fR \fIBY\fR
Who closes / revokes it.
.TP
\fB\-\-host\-dir\fR \fIHOST_DIR\fR
Host directory of the agents' /workspace mount (default: $ACC_WORKSPACE_HOST_DIR).
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli mission revoke\fR \fImission_id\fR [\fB\-\-by\fR \fIBY\fR] [\fB\-\-host\-dir\fR \fIHOST_DIR\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Revoke a mission now.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-by\fR \fIBY\fR
Who closes / revokes it.
.TP
\fB\-\-host\-dir\fR \fIHOST_DIR\fR
Host directory of the agents' /workspace mount (default: $ACC_WORKSPACE_HOST_DIR).
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli mission purge\fR \fImission_id\fR [\fB\-\-by\fR \fIBY\fR] [\fB\-\-host\-dir\fR \fIHOST_DIR\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Delete the items a mission backed up (the final allowance).
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-by\fR \fIBY\fR
Who closes / revokes it.
.TP
\fB\-\-host\-dir\fR \fIHOST_DIR\fR
Host directory of the agents' /workspace mount (default: $ACC_WORKSPACE_HOST_DIR).
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli mission restore\fR \fImission_id\fR [\fB\-\-by\fR \fIBY\fR] [\fB\-\-host\-dir\fR \fIHOST_DIR\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Put the items a mission backed up back where they were.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-by\fR \fIBY\fR
Who closes / revokes it.
.TP
\fB\-\-host\-dir\fR \fIHOST_DIR\fR
Host directory of the agents' /workspace mount (default: $ACC_WORKSPACE_HOST_DIR).
.RE
.SS "oversight"
Inspect and drive the oversight queue.
.TP
\fBacc-cli oversight pending\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR] [\fB\-\-watch\fR]
List pending oversight items.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-watch\fR
Tail the arbiter HEARTBEAT and re-print on each update.
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli oversight submit\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR] \fB\-\-task\-id\fR \fITASK_ID\fR \fB\-\-agent\-id\fR \fIAGENT_ID\fR [\fB\-\-risk\fR \fI{HIGH,UNACCEPTABLE}\fR] \fIsummary [summary ...]\fR
Submit a synthetic oversight item.
.RS
.TP
\fIsummary [summary ...]\fR
Human-readable summary (positional, may include spaces).
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli oversight approve\fR \fIoversight_id\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR] [\fB\-\-approver\-id\fR \fIAPPROVER_ID\fR]
Publish OVERSIGHT_DECISION APPROVE.
.TP
\fBacc-cli oversight reject\fR \fIoversight_id\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR] [\fB\-\-approver\-id\fR \fIAPPROVER_ID\fR] [\fB\-\-reason\fR \fIREASON\fR]
Publish OVERSIGHT_DECISION REJECT.
.TP
\fBacc-cli oversight delegate\fR \fIoversight_id\fR \fB\-\-to\fR \fITO\fR [\fB\-\-note\fR \fINOTE\fR] [\fB\-c\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR] [\fB\-\-approver\-id\fR \fIAPPROVER_ID\fR]
Hand a pending decision to a person or a tier (it stays PENDING).
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR \fITO\fR
A person (webgui:alice, slack:U1) or a tier (operator).
.TP
\fB\-\-note\fR \fINOTE\fR
Why, for whoever picks it up.
.RE
.SS "plan"
Submit and monitor PLAN signals.
.TP
\fBacc-cli plan submit\fR \fIplan_file\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR] [\fB\-\-watch\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\-s\fR \fITIMEOUT_S\fR]
Submit a PLAN payload from a JSON file (or stdin).
.RS
.TP
\fIplan_file\fR
Path to the JSON file. Use '-' to read from stdin.
.TP
\fB\-\-collective\fR, \fB\-c\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR
Override the plan's collective_id (default: payload value or $ACC_COLLECTIVE_ID).
.TP
\fB\-\-watch\fR
After submit, stream PLAN re-broadcasts until terminal state.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\-s\fR \fITIMEOUT_S\fR
Watch timeout in seconds (only with --watch; default 300).
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli plan watch\fR \fIplan_id\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\-s\fR \fITIMEOUT_S\fR]
Watch the PLAN broadcast for a known plan_id.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-collective\fR, \fB\-c\fR \fICOLLECTIVE\fR
Collective id (default: $ACC_COLLECTIVE_ID).
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\-s\fR \fITIMEOUT_S\fR
Watch timeout in seconds (default 600 \[u2014] Ctrl-C also stops).
.RE
.SS "profile"
Named deployment profiles.
.TP
\fBacc-cli profile list\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Show available profiles and the active one.
.TP
\fBacc-cli profile show\fR \fIname\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Print a profile.
.TP
\fBacc-cli profile diff\fR \fIname\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
What applying it would change.
.TP
\fBacc-cli profile validate\fR \fIname\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Check it without applying it.
.TP
\fBacc-cli profile apply\fR \fIname\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
Validate, then apply.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show changes, write nothing.
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli profile revert\fR
Undo the last apply.
.TP
\fBacc-cli profile export\fR \fIname\fR [\fB\-\-out\fR \fIOUT\fR]
Emit a portable profile document.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR \fIOUT\fR
Write to a file instead of stdout.
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli profile import\fR \fIpath\fR [\fB\-\-overwrite\fR]
Install an exported profile (does not apply it).
.SS "instance"
Instances: a collective bound to an owner, a posture and its own state.
.TP
\fBacc-cli instance list\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Instances on this host.
.TP
\fBacc-cli instance show\fR \fIid\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
One instance: record, roots, collective definition.
.TP
\fBacc-cli instance create\fR \fIid\fR [\fB\-\-owner\fR \fIOWNER\fR] [\fB\-\-profile\fR \fIPROFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-hub\fR \fIHUB\fR] [\fB\-\-pack\fR \fIPACK\fR] [\fB\-\-agent\fR \fIAGENT\fR] [\fB\-\-stack\-profile\fR \fISTACK_PROFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-note\fR \fINOTE\fR]
Create an instance (record + collective definition + state roots).
.RS
.TP
\fIid\fR
The instance id \[u2014] it is the collective id (a DNS label).
.TP
\fB\-\-owner\fR \fIOWNER\fR
source:subject (default: the principal running this command).
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fIPROFILE\fR
Deployment profile (posture) the instance runs under.
.TP
\fB\-\-hub\fR \fIHUB\fR
Hub collective id; omit for standalone.
.TP
\fB\-\-pack\fR \fIPACK\fR
@scope/name@constraint (repeatable) \[u2014] the installed set.
.TP
\fB\-\-agent\fR \fIAGENT\fR
Domain role to run (repeatable).
.TP
\fB\-\-stack\-profile\fR \fISTACK_PROFILE\fR
Control set: edge-min | edge | full | dc (default edge).
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli instance archive\fR \fIid\fR
Mark an instance archived (state stays; forget is erasure).
.TP
\fBacc-cli instance export\fR \fIid\fR [\fB\-\-out\fR \fIOUT\fR]
Emit a portable instance document (definition, never state).
.TP
\fBacc-cli instance import\fR \fIpath\fR [\fB\-\-owner\fR \fIOWNER\fR] [\fB\-\-id\fR \fIID\fR]
Create an instance from an exported document, owned here.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-owner\fR \fIOWNER\fR
source:subject (default: the principal running this command).
.TP
\fB\-\-id\fR \fIID\fR
New instance id (default: the document's).
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli instance synth\fR \fIid\fR [\fB\-\-out\fR \fIOUT\fR] [\fB\-\-image\fR \fIIMAGE\fR]
Render the podman-compose overlay that runs the instance with its roots.
.TP
\fBacc-cli instance env\fR \fIid\fR
Shell environment for the surfaces (TUI, acc-cli) to attach to the instance.
.SS "up"
Start the container stack (acc-deploy.sh up).
.PP
\fBacc-cli up\fR
.SS "down"
Stop the container stack (acc-deploy.sh down).
.PP
\fBacc-cli down\fR
.SS "restart"
Re-create the stack on the current images (acc-deploy.sh restart).
.PP
\fBacc-cli restart\fR
.SS "stack"
Any acc-deploy.sh verb (build, rebuild, ps, logs, ...).
.PP
\fBacc-cli stack\fR
.SS "schedule"
Manage recurring task schedules (proposal 005).
.TP
\fBacc-cli schedule add\fR \fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR \fB\-\-role\fR \fIROLE\fR \fB\-\-task\fR \fITASK\fR \fB\-\-cron\fR \fICRON\fR [\fB\-\-collective\-id\fR \fICOLLECTIVE_ID\fR] [\fB\-\-target\-agent\-id\fR \fITARGET_AGENT_ID\fR] [\fB\-\-root\fR \fIROOT\fR]
Register a new schedule.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-task\fR \fITASK\fR
Task description.
.TP
\fB\-\-cron\fR \fICRON\fR
Cron expression \[u2014] supports `* * * * *`, `*/N * * * *`, `M * * * *`, `0 H * * *`, `M H * * *`.
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fIROOT\fR
Schedules dir override.
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli schedule list\fR [\fB\-\-root\fR \fIROOT\fR]
List schedules.
.TP
\fBacc-cli schedule remove\fR \fIname\fR [\fB\-\-root\fR \fIROOT\fR]
Remove a schedule.
.TP
\fBacc-cli schedule run-once\fR [\fB\-\-root\fR \fIROOT\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
Fire any due schedules and exit.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Don't publish; just print what would fire.
.RE
.SS "e2e"
Golden-prompt suite \[u2014] list, validate, run, show.
.TP
\fBacc-cli e2e list\fR [\fB\-\-root\fR \fIROOT\fR]
List known golden prompts (no network access).
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fIROOT\fR
Override the golden-prompts directory (default: examples/golden_prompts).
.RE
.TP
\fBacc-cli e2e validate\fR [\fB\-\-root\fR \fIROOT\fR]
Schema-check every YAML under the golden-prompts root.
.TP
\fBacc-cli e2e show\fR \fIname\fR [\fB\-\-root\fR \fIROOT\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR \fI{yaml,json}\fR]
Print one prompt's full definition.
.TP
\fBacc-cli e2e run\fR \fI[name]\fR [\fB\-\-root\fR \fIROOT\fR] [\fB\-\-collective\-id\fR \fICOLLECTIVE_ID\fR] [\fB\-\-nats\-url\fR \fINATS_URL\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-history\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-loop\fR \fISECONDS\fR]
Execute one or all prompts against a live NATS stack.
.RS
.TP
\fI[name]\fR
Prompt name to run. Omit to run every prompt.
.TP
\fB\-\-collective\-id\fR \fICOLLECTIVE_ID\fR
Override ACC_COLLECTIVE_ID for this run.
.TP
\fB\-\-nats\-url\fR \fINATS_URL\fR
Override ACC_NATS_URL for this run.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit results as JSON (one object per prompt) \[u2014] useful for ingestion by the scheduled maintenance agent.
.TP
\fB\-\-history\fR \fIPATH\fR
Append one JSONL row per result to PATH (e.g. test/history/golden.jsonl). Builds a regression archive across scheduled runs.
.TP
\fB\-\-loop\fR \fISECONDS\fR
Re-run the suite every SECONDS (scheduled mode). Runs forever until interrupted; combine with --history to accrue a trend. Omit for a single run.
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ACC_NATS_URL
NATS endpoint for every bus command (default \fBnats://localhost:4222\fR).
.TP
.B ACC_COLLECTIVE_ID
Default collective for the bus and oversight commands (default \fBsol\-01\fR).
.TP
.B ACC_CONFIG_PATH
The \fBacc\-config.yaml\fR to read; otherwise found through the host layout
described in
.BR acc (1).
.TP
.BR ACC_ROLES_ROOT ", " ACC_SKILLS_ROOT ", " ACC_MCPS_ROOT
The role, skill and MCP trees; otherwise the share tree of the layout.
.TP
.BR ACC_HOME ", " ACC_SHARE ", " ACC_STATE
Override the configuration, data and state roots; see
.BR acc (1).
.TP
.B ACC_PACKAGES_ROOT
Where installed packages live (default \fB/var/lib/acc/packages\fR).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/acc/acc\-config.yaml
The system configuration (an RPM install); \fI~/.config/acc/acc\-config.yaml\fR
for a per-user one.
.TP
.I /etc/acc/acc.env
Secrets for the stack, mode 0640 root:acc.
.B acc-cli secrets
and
.B acc-cli auth
report names only, never values.
.TP
.I ~/.config/acc/trust.yaml
Trusted workspace directories, managed by
.BR "acc-cli workspace" .
.TP
.I /var/lib/acc
Shared state: packages, instances, workspaces, sessions, trace.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; non-zero when the action failed or found a fault (for
example \fBdoctor\fR and \fBconfig check\fR exit non-zero on a finding);
130 when interrupted with Ctrl-C.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
acc\-cli doctor                       # deployment health, read-only
acc\-cli status                       # per-agent and collective health
acc\-cli role list
acc\-cli oversight pending
acc\-cli oversight approve <oversight_id>
acc\-cli nats sub 'acc.sol\-01.>'
acc\-cli trace <task_id> \-\-limit 100
acc\-cli config set \-\-dry\-run llm.backend openai_compat
acc\-cli collective diff               # spec vs. running containers
acc\-cli doctor \-\-paths              # where this host's ACC lives
.fi
